<DocPage eyebrow="CHANGELOG / V1.1.0" title="v1.1.0" lead="Changes since v1.0.10: additional observations, richer failure investigation, and semantic comparisons alongside the existing UI automation and World searches." description="Verified additions, behavior changes, fixes, and version-specific limits between Gua v1.0.10 and v1.1.0." section="changelog">
  <h2>Versions compared</h2><p>The preceding published release is v1.0.10. This page is based on the tagged source comparison and the v1.1.0 release notes. <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/compare/gua-v1.0.10...gua-v1.1.0">v1.0.10 → v1.1.0</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/releases/tag/gua-v1.1.0">Release</a></p>
  <p>UI queries/actions, World Object Tree, game input, Visual comparison, sequential Recording, MCP/WebMCP, and Godot/Unity integrations already existed. They are not new in 1.1.0. For installation, see the regular guides: <a href="/docs/dotnet-packages/">.NET packages</a> · <a href="/docs/npm-packages/">npm packages</a></p>
  <h2 id="snapshots">Added: semantic snapshot comparisons</h2><p>Visual tests already compared PNGs. 1.1.0 adds Gua.Testing.Snapshots to compare UI/World IDs, hierarchy, text, and values against saved baselines.</p><p><a href="/docs/dotnet-packages/#semantic-snapshots">Installation and comparison example</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/149">#149</a></p>
  <h2 id="observe">Added: typed values and additional observations</h2><p>Games can now register custom values and expose reads and change notifications alongside standard UI/World data. Shared Value types, enum catalogs, and equality were added across the C ABI, C++, .NET, and gua-value-tools.</p><p><a href="/docs/gua-runtime/#observe">Register and read observations</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/139">#139</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/141">#141</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/144">#144</a></p>
  <h2 id="trace">Added: Trace records and offline reports</h2><p>Trace records operations, completion, observations, assertions, and attachments together. Inspector opens it offline; GuaTraceReport.WriteHtml creates a standalone report. Existing Recording replay serves a different purpose.</p><p><a href="/godot/testing/#trace">Capture and report examples</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/140">#140</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/146">#146</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/157">#157</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/169">#169</a></p>
  <h2 id="locators">Changed: resolve targets when acting and wait for readiness</h2><p>Queries and Get already existed. Locator actions now re-resolve the target and wait for conditions such as visibility and enabled state before acting. Use Query(...).ClickAsync() rather than retaining a node from an earlier screen.</p><p><a href="/godot/testing/#locators">Locator action example</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/142">#142</a></p>
  <h2 id="lint">Added: explicit checks of published structure</h2><p>GuaSemanticLinter.Analyze checks issues such as duplicate IDs or invalid hierarchy when explicitly requested. It does not run automatically on every frame.</p><p><a href="/semantic-ui-tree/#lint">Lint usage</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/150">#150</a></p>
  <h2 id="spatial">Added: queries against engine physics</h2><p>World coordinate searches already existed. 1.1.0 adds bounded physics queries such as raycasts for Godot/Unity, with explicit Testing/Debug authorization. Built-in public browser AI paths do not support them.</p><p><a href="/world-object-tree/#physics">Difference from World searches</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/151">#151</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/156">#156</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/159">#159</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/161">#161</a></p>
  <h2 id="input">Added: input value descriptions and timed replay</h2><p>Opt-in v2 tools describe accepted input values and examples. ReplayTimedSegmentAsync executes a finite, scheduled input plan. Sequential Recording already existed; built-in MCP/Inspector replay remains sequential.</p><p><a href="/game-input/#metadata">Input metadata guide</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/152">#152</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/160">#160</a></p>
  <h2 id="distribution">Added: offline resources for test records</h2><p>Gua.Testing embeds schemas and an offline Viewer and can generate Trace HTML reports without a separate Node or Bun installation.</p><p><a href="/docs/dotnet-packages/">.NET packages</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/163">#163</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/176">#176</a></p>
  <h2 id="inspector">Added: generate C# tests in Inspector</h2><p>Generate Gua.Testing locators, actions, and assertions from a selected UI node. Review the ID and expected state before adding the code to a test.</p><p><a href="/inspector/#codegen">Generation steps</a> · <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/148">#148</a></p>
  <h2 id="fixes">Behavior fixes</h2><ul><li>Fixed Unity UI Toolkit Button clicks and Tab navigation. <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/137">#137</a></li><li>Fixed empty game-input search responses in Godot Web. <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/138">#138</a></li><li>MCP retains an unconfirmed outcome on disconnect for submitted actions, instead of treating them as never sent. <a href="https://github.com/gua-project/gua/pull/165">#165</a></li></ul>
  <h2 id="support">Limits at 1.1.0</h2><p>Unity 6000.5.3f1 desktop Mono Players were verified on Windows, Linux, Intel Mac, and Apple Silicon Mac. Editor was verified on Windows, Linux, and Apple M4; native Intel Mac Editor was implemented but unverified. Built-in browser screenshot/privileged spatial queries are unsupported; simultaneous native MCP/WebMCP routing in Codex was unverified. This historical page does not incorporate later 1.1.1 verification.</p><p><a href="/docs/unity-reference/">Detailed engine support</a> · <a href="/webmcp/">Browser limits</a></p>
</DocPage>
